WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:11.117
Later that day Ally was clearing off a table when she spotted Barry slipping the spring through his finger again.

2
00:00:11.118 --> 00:00:16.813
"Barry!" she snapped. "I asked you not to practice at the diner anymore."

3
00:00:16.814 --> 00:00:20.018
"Sorry," he said.

4
00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:32.028
But as soon as Ally turned her back, Barry put a plate of eggs on the spring, tripped, and spilled eggs all over the floor.

5
00:00:32.029 --> 00:00:39.137
"That's the third plate you've dropped today! Plus the bowl of cereal that landed on a customer!"

6
00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:46.071
Ally was trying not to get angry, but his tricks were causing problems.

7
00:00:46.072 --> 00:00:51.923
"Go on home. I'll clean up."

8
00:00:51.924 --> 00:00:56.930
Ally had just finished cleaning up when Mateo arrived.

9
00:00:56.931 --> 00:01:01.602
"Did you find my pod at the museum?" Ally asked eagerly.

10
00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:10.289
"No." Mateo looked upset. "I overheard Dr. Lloyd saying that he hasn't found the ship he lured to Earth yet.

11
00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:13.530
But it's just a matter of time until he does!"

12
00:01:13.531 --> 00:01:19.535
Ally gulped. "Dr. Lloyd will never give up looking for me!"

13
00:01:19.536 --> 00:01:23.507
"At least we know he doesn't have your ship," Mateo said.

14
00:01:23.508 --> 00:01:29.369
Ally drummed her fingers on the counter. "But who does?"

15
00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:33.569
"Excuse me." Randy stuck his head out of the kitchen.

16
00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:40.159
"Is Barry gone?" When they nodded, he came out.

17
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:47.891
"I saw Barry taking pictures of the food delivery today. It was weird."

18
00:01:47.892 --> 00:01:53.112
He scratched his head. "I'm worried that kid is up to something."

19
00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:58.268
"Hmm," Mateo said. "We'll keep an eye on him."

20
00:01:58.269 --> 00:02:04.258
Randy gave a thumbs-up and returned to the kitchen.

21
00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:10.126
"Barry keeps causing trouble," Ally said. "Do you think he knows my secret?"

22
00:02:10.127 --> 00:02:14.629
"No," Mateo said. "He's just odd."

23
00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:18.967
"When I read his mind, he's always thinking about his dad.

24
00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:21.535
So maybe he's not suspicious of me."

25
00:02:21.536 --> 00:02:24.954
Mateo changed the subject. "Ready to head home?"

26
00:02:24.955 --> 00:02:31.310
"Yes," Ally said. "It's been a long day."

27
00:02:31.311 --> 00:02:36.122
After Ally and Mateo left the diner, they walked by the heart sculpture.

28
00:02:36.123 --> 00:02:39.470
"Oh! That reminds me," Ally said.

29
00:02:39.471 --> 00:02:43.555
"I promised the artist that I'd stop by the park to see her work."

30
00:02:43.556 --> 00:02:51.438
"Sounds fun, let's go," Mateo said.

31
00:02:51.439 --> 00:02:55.420
But entering the park reminded Ally of her lost pod again.

32
00:02:55.421 --> 00:02:59.463
"I wish I knew where my pod was," she said.

33
00:02:59.464 --> 00:03:04.216
"And I can't believe I'm saying this, but I really miss Alpha."

34
00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:11.060
"We'll find them," Mateo said. "Hey, look over there—there's a new sculpture."

35
00:03:11.061 --> 00:03:17.392
He pointed to a large metal ball sitting in the middle of a lawn.

36
00:03:17.393 --> 00:03:23.527
Sarah waved. "I'm glad you made it.

37
00:03:23.528 --> 00:03:31.647
I know this doesn't look like much yet, but it's going to be a giant model of Earth, as seen from space."

38
00:03:31.648 --> 00:03:36.931
Ally inspected the ball.

39
00:03:36.932 --> 00:03:41.760
"It would be cool if you could make it spin on its axis."

40
00:03:41.761 --> 00:03:45.371
"Another great idea!" Sarah said.

41
00:03:45.372 --> 00:03:50.009
Ally smiled. "My parents always told me to be helpful . . ."

42
00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:52.464
Ally stopped when she heard a high-pitched ping.

43
00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:58.094
It was faint, and she wasn't sure where it was coming from, but she'd know that sound anywhere.

44
00:03:58.095 --> 00:04:02.700
Ping . . . ping . . . It was an Astralian distress signal!

45
00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:08.806
As soon as she could, Ally whispered to Mateo to keep Sarah busy for a few minutes.

46
00:04:08.807 --> 00:04:12.900
Then she followed the sound around the metal model of Earth.

47
00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:20.314
On one side of the sculpture, she suddenly spotted something familiar—Astralian symbols.

48
00:04:20.315 --> 00:04:24.463
She stepped closer and let out a startled gasp.

49
00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:29.563
This model of Earth was made from cut-up pieces of metal—from her pod!

50
00:04:29.564 --> 00:04:32.040
Ping . . . ping!

51
00:04:32.041 --> 00:04:35.290
Even worse, that distress signal was coming from Alpha!

52
00:04:35.291 --> 00:04:39.143
"I'm coming, Alpha!" Ally whispered.

53
00:04:39.144 --> 00:04:46.512
She crawled inside a hole in the huge hollow ball, which was filled with all kinds of junk and broken technology.

54
00:04:46.513 --> 00:04:49.991
"Where are you?"

55
00:04:49.992 --> 00:04:54.219
Alpha's signal was fading as Ally frantically weeded through the junk.

56
00:04:54.220 --> 00:05:06.401
Then she spotted a motherboard with Astralian symbols. "Alpha!"

57
00:05:06.402 --> 00:05:15.892
Ally crawled out of the sculpture, clutching the motherboard.

58
00:05:15.893 --> 00:05:20.234
Sarah beamed when she saw Ally.

59
00:05:20.235 --> 00:05:25.788
"That's exactly what I want kids to do—remove junk from Earth!

60
00:05:25.789 --> 00:05:33.567
You see, my art is a metaphor for how we're polluting our planet, creating mounds of junk.

61
00:05:33.568 --> 00:05:36.249
Oh, and you found the source of that noise too.

62
00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:45.129
Thank goodness! It's been driving me crazy. You can keep that object, I mean, if you want it."

63
00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:49.145
"I do want it," Ally said, "very badly!"

64
00:05:49.146 --> 00:05:55.779
Ally and Mateo said good-bye to Sarah and rushed away.

65
00:05:55.780 --> 00:06:00.703
"We have to hurry, Mateo," Ally said. "Alpha's signal is fading fast.

66
00:06:00.704 --> 00:06:10.853
If we don't get her connected to a power source soon, we could lose her forever!"

